  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Results for $[4,1,0]^2$ (2026-10-02, P1 $=(h,\\theta)=(1/2,\\{2/7,-3/5\\})$, 200 digits, full run about 25 s)\n- **Checks.** The quantum determinant, commutativity and $\\Omega$ eigen-covector checks pass to $\\le10^{-189}$. The chain identity $d\\cdot(R\\otimes R)\\Psi=q$ holds to $10^{-155}$. There are 15 HW states: 11 sectors, with multiplicity 2 at $[7,2,1]$, $[6,3,1]$ and $[5,4,1]$.\n- **Site-1 localization (new; Section 4).** For $\\lambda_1\\le4$ and $c=-6..1$, the nontrivial site-1-local shapes are exactly **$T_{(1,1)},T_{(2,2)},T_{(3,3)},T_{(4,3)}$ at $\\theta_1-4h$**. That is *four* shapes: the pattern \"$T_{(1,1)}$ plus $T_{(k,\\lambda_1-\\lambda_2)}$, $k=\\lambda_1-\\lambda_2..\\lambda_1$\" predicted only $T_{(1,1)},T_{(3,3)},T_{(4,3)}$ and **misses $T_{(2,2)}$**. No shape is site-2 local or an eigen-covector in this range.\n- **Prefactors** (fitted at P1; each ansatz match is unique; checked at P2 to $10^{-190}$):\n  - $f_{(1,1)}=(\\theta_{12}-3h)(\\theta_{12}-5h)$;\n  - $f_{(2,2)}=(\\theta_{12}-2h)(\\theta_{12}-3h)(\\theta_{12}-4h)(\\theta_{12}-5h)$;\n  - $f_{(3,3)}=(\\theta_{12}-h)(\\theta_{12}-2h)(\\theta_{12}-3h)^2(\\theta_{12}-4h)(\\theta_{12}-5h)$;\n  - $f_{(4,3)}=(\\theta_{12}-h)^2(\\theta_{12}-2h)(\\theta_{12}-3h)^2(\\theta_{12}-4h)(\\theta_{12}-5h)$.\n- **Structural.** The contamination ratios of all 14 non-top HW states are $\\varphi,\\omega$-independent, with spread $\\le1.3\\times10^{-4}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-5}$.\n- **End to end, site 1 + $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ only.** All 14 non-top HW states are recovered from Q-side numbers, scale included. Relative errors are $10^{-3.8}$–$10^{-5.2}$ at $(10^{-4},\\varphi)$ and $10^{-4.7}$–$10^{-6.3}$ at $(10^{-5},\\varphi')$, i.e. $O(\\varepsilon)$, with $\\ge123$ correct digits.\n  - **Sector-wide cleaning is enough** for every sector except $[6,3,1]$. That includes $[7,2,1]$ (HW rank 2, second singular value 0.0069 at both $\\varepsilon=10^{-4}$ and $10^{-5}$, so small but genuine), $[5,4,1]$ (second singular value 0.16) and the bottom irrep $[4,4,2]$.\n  - **$[6,3,1]$ (multiplicity 2) needs per-copy cleaning.** The sector clean space is 2-dimensional with HW rank 1; each copy's own clean space is 3-dimensional.\n- **Caveats.** The clean coefficients are fitted numerically, not in closed form. There is one chain point for the pipeline (P2 was used only for the $f$'s). The eigenvalues are read from the eigenvectors and stand in for the Q's.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
